IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hesa-formulas`

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003, ss 36-45, 128-15, 128C-10, 140-10(1A), 154-1, 154-20, 154-25, 198-10, 198-15 -- worked
-- cases for hesa-formulas.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- text and the sidecar formulas before running. CPI index numbers (December 2024 to 2027: 132, 136, 140, 139) and AWE figures
-- ($3,800 for 2025-26, $4,000 for 2026-27) are ILLUSTRATIVE; the s 128-20 limit is taken as in force from 1 January 2026, an
-- assumption. No result here is a figure in force.

`illustrative December CPI` MEANS LIST 132, 136, 140, 139

§ `s 140-10(1A) -- a reduced indexation factor`

-- A = 1.032, B = 100 days: 1 + (0.032 / 365) x 265 = 1.02323, so 1.023. B = 0: 1.032. B = 365 (the whole year): 1.
#ASSERT `What is my reduced HELP debt indexation factor` 1.032 100 EQUALS 1.023
#ASSERT `What is my reduced HELP debt indexation factor` 1.032 0 EQUALS 1.032
#ASSERT `What is my reduced HELP debt indexation factor` 1.032 365 EQUALS 1

§ `ss 198-10, 198-15 -- Part 5-6 indexation`

-- 136 / 132 = 1.0303: 1.030. The Act's own example: 1.102795 is rounded up to 1.103.
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 indexation factor` 136 132 EQUALS 1.03
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 indexation factor` 110.2795 100 EQUALS 1.103
-- $106,319 x 1.030 = $109,508.57, rounded down: $109,508. A factor of 1 or less leaves it alone.
#ASSERT `What does a Part 5-6 amount become on 1 January` 106319 136 132 EQUALS 109508
#ASSERT `What does a Part 5-6 amount become on 1 January` 106319 130 131 EQUALS 106319

-- From $106,319 in 2026: 1 January 2027 uses December 2026 (140) over December 2025 (136), 1.029: $109,402.25, so $109,402.
-- 1 January 2028: 139 / 140 is below 1: still $109,402. 1 January 2029 needs December 2028: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` 106319 2026 2026 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 106319
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` 106319 2026 2027 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 109402
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` 106319 2026 2028 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 109402
#ASSERT `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` 106319 2026 2029 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS NOTHING
-- With $20,000 already borrowed: $109,402 - $20,000 = $89,402 left in 2027.
#ASSERT `How much can I still borrow on the indexed limit` FALSE 2026 2027 `illustrative December CPI` 20000 0 EQUALS JUST 89402

§ `ss 154-1, 154-20, 154-25 -- repayment thresholds from AWE`

-- 2026-27: $67,000 x 4,000 / 3,800 = $70,526.32, down to $70,526; $125,000 x 4,000 / 3,800 = $131,578.95, down to $131,578.
#ASSERT `What is my minimum repayment income from AWE` 2026 4000 3800 EQUALS JUST 70526
#ASSERT `What is the upper repayment threshold from AWE` 2026 4000 3800 EQUALS JUST 131578
#ASSERT `What is my minimum repayment income from AWE` 2025 3800 3800 EQUALS JUST 67000
#ASSERT `What is my minimum repayment income from AWE` 2024 3800 3800 EQUALS NOTHING
-- $90,000 in 2026-27 with a $50,000 debt: 15% of ($90,000 - $70,526) = $2,921.10, less than 10% ($9,000) and the debt.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory HELP repayment must I make from AWE` 2026 4000 3800 90000 50000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 2921.1
-- The same income in 2025-26: 15% of $23,000 = $3,450.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory HELP repayment must I make from AWE` 2025 3800 3800 90000 50000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 3450
-- $70,000 in 2026-27 is under the $70,526 minimum: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much compulsory HELP repayment must I make from AWE` 2026 4000 3800 70000 50000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0

§ `ss 36-45, 128C-10 -- the most I can be charged`

-- A maximum of $16,992 a place, a unit of 0.125 EFTSL: $2,124.
#ASSERT `What is the most my provider may charge for the unit` 16992 0.125 EQUALS 2124
-- $18,001 for one EFTSL, a course of 0.5 EFTSL: $9,000.50, rounded down to $9,000 (s 128C-10(2)).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be charged for an accelerator program course` 18001 0.5 EQUALS 9000
